# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CHSH game {#the-chsh-game}"
msgstr "El juego CHSH {#the-chsh-game}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"El último ejemplo que veremos en esta lección no es un protocolo, sino un *juego* conocido como el\n"
"*juego CHSH*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando hablamos de un juego en este contexto, no nos referimos a algo pensado para divertirse o competir, sino a una abstracción matemática en el sentido de la *teoría de juegos*.\n"
"Las abstracciones matemáticas de juegos se estudian en economía y ciencias de la computación, por ejemplo, y son a la vez fascinantes y útiles.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las letras CHSH hacen referencia a los autores — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony y Richard Holt — de un artículo de 1969 donde se describió el ejemplo por primera vez.\n"
"Ellos no lo describieron como un juego, sino como un experimento.\n"
"Sin embargo, su descripción como juego es natural e intuitiva.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"El juego CHSH pertenece a una clase de juegos conocidos como *juegos no locales*.\n"
"Los juegos no locales son increíblemente interesantes y tienen conexiones profundas con la física, las ciencias de la computación y las matemáticas — guardando misterios que aún permanecen sin resolver.\n"
"Comenzaremos la sección explicando qué son los juegos no locales y luego nos centraremos en el juego CHSH y en lo que lo hace interesante.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "Juegos no locales {#nonlocal-games}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un juego no local es un *juego cooperativo* donde dos jugadores, Alice y Bob, trabajan juntos para lograr un resultado particular.\n"
"El juego está dirigido por un *árbitro*, que actúa según reglas estrictas conocidas por Alice y Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice y Bob pueden prepararse para el juego como deseen, pero una vez que comienza, tienen *prohibido comunicarse*.\n"
"Podemos imaginar el juego tomando lugar en algún tipo de instalación segura — como si el árbitro jugara el papel de un detective y Alice y Bob fueran sospechosos siendo interrogados en habitaciones separadas.\n"
"Pero otra forma de pensar en la configuración es que Alice y Bob están separados por una gran distancia, y la comunicación está prohibida porque la velocidad de la luz no lo permite dentro del tiempo de ejecución del juego.\n"
"Es decir, si Alice intenta enviar un mensaje a Bob, el juego habrá terminado antes de que él lo reciba, y viceversa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks Alice and Bob one question each.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"La forma en que funciona un juego no local es que el árbitro primero le hace una pregunta a cada uno.\n"
"Usaremos la letra $x$ para referirnos a la pregunta de Alice e $y$ para referirnos a la de Bob.\n"
"Aquí estamos pensando en $x$ e $y$ como estados clásicos, y en el juego CHSH $x$ e $y$ son bits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"El árbitro usa *aleatoriedad* para seleccionar estas preguntas.\n"
"Para ser precisos, existe una probabilidad $p(x,y)$ asociada con cada par posible $(x,y)$ de preguntas, y el árbitro se ha comprometido a elegir las preguntas aleatoriamente, en el momento del juego, de esta manera.\n"
"Todos, incluyendo Alice y Bob, conocen estas probabilidades — pero nadie sabe específicamente qué par $(x,y)$ será elegido hasta que comience el juego.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b.$\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Después de que Alice y Bob reciben sus preguntas, deben proporcionar respuestas: la respuesta de Alice es $a$ y la de Bob es $b.$\n"
"De nuevo, estos son estados clásicos en general, y bits en el juego CHSH.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"En este punto el árbitro toma una decisión: Alice y Bob *ganan* o *pierden* dependiendo de si el par de respuestas $(a,b)$ es considerado correcto para el par de preguntas $(x,y)$ según un conjunto fijo de reglas.\n"
"Distintas reglas significan distintos juegos, y las reglas del juego CHSH en particular se describen en la sección siguiente.\n"
"Como ya se sugirió, las reglas son conocidas por todos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the "
"interactions.\n"
msgstr ""
"El siguiente diagrama ofrece una representación gráfica de las "
"interacciones.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Juego no local](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically "
"the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that "
"makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding "
"suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr ""
"La incertidumbre sobre qué preguntas se harán, y específicamente el hecho de"
" que cada jugador desconoce la pregunta del otro, es lo que hace que los "
"juegos no locales sean un desafío para Alice y Bob — igual que sospechosos "
"que conspiran en habitaciones separadas intentando mantener una historia "
"coherente.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Una descripción precisa del árbitro define una instancia de un juego no local.\n"
"Esto incluye una especificación de las probabilidades $p(x,y)$ para cada par de preguntas junto con las reglas\n"
"que determinan si cada par de respuestas $(a,b)$ gana o pierde para cada par de preguntas posible $(x,y).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"In fact, it's extremely interesting; there are some pretty simple nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the surprisingly unintuitive nature of the nonlocal games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Veremos el juego CHSH en un momento, pero antes reconozcamos brevemente que también es interesante considerar otros juegos no locales.\n"
"De hecho, es extremadamente interesante; hay algunos juegos no locales bastante simples para los cuales actualmente se desconoce qué tan bien pueden jugar Alice y Bob usando entrelazamiento.\n"
"La configuración es sencilla, pero hay complejidad en juego — y para algunos juegos puede ser imposiblemente difícil calcular las mejores estrategias o estrategias cercanas a las óptimas para Alice y Bob.\n"
"Esta es la naturaleza sorprendentemente contraintuitiva del modelo de juegos no locales.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "Descripción del juego CHSH {#chsh-game-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is "
"Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is "
"Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí está la descripción precisa del juego CHSH, donde (como antes) $x$ es "
"la pregunta de Alice, $y$ es la pregunta de Bob, $a$ es la respuesta de "
"Alice y $b$ es la respuesta de Bob:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
msgstr "Las preguntas y respuestas son todas bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, "
"each of the four possibilities, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ and $(1,1),$ is "
"selected with probability $1/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"El árbitro elige las preguntas $(x,y)$ *uniformemente al azar*. Es decir, "
"cada una de las cuatro posibilidades, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ y $(1,1),$ "
"se selecciona con probabilidad $1/4.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by"
" listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each "
"pair of questions $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Las respuestas $(a,b)$ *ganan* para las preguntas $(x,y)$ si $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ y *pierden* en caso contrario. La siguiente tabla expresa esta "
"regla listando las condiciones de victoria y derrota sobre las respuestas "
"$(a,b)$ para cada par de preguntas $(x,y).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr ""
"Limitación de las estrategias clásicas {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning "
"with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora consideremos estrategias para Alice y Bob en el juego CHSH, comenzando"
" con las estrategias *clásicas*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "Estrategias deterministas {#deterministic-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0,$ and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Empezaremos con las estrategias *deterministas*, donde la respuesta $a$ de Alice es una función de la pregunta $x$ que recibe, y del mismo modo la respuesta $b$ de Bob es una función de la pregunta $y$ que él recibe.\n"
"Así, por ejemplo, podemos escribir $a(0)$ para representar la respuesta de Alice cuando su pregunta es $0,$ y $a(1)$ para representar su respuesta cuando su pregunta es $1.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to understand this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered in the lesson on [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) — and so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ninguna estrategia determinista puede ganar el juego CHSH todas las veces.\n"
"Una manera de entender esto es simplemente ir uno por uno a través de todas las estrategias deterministas posibles y verificar que cada una pierde para al menos uno de los cuatro pares de preguntas posibles.\n"
"Alice y Bob pueden elegir entre cuatro funciones posibles de un bit a un bit — que encontramos en la lección sobre [Sistemas individuales](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) — y por eso hay $16$ estrategias deterministas diferentes en total que verificar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1),$ then $a(0) = b(1);$ and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"También podemos razonarlo analíticamente.\n"
"Si la estrategia de Alice y Bob gana cuando $(x,y) = (0,0),$ entonces debe ser que $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"si su estrategia gana cuando $(x,y) = (0,1),$ entonces $a(0) = b(1);$ y del mismo modo,\n"
"si la estrategia gana para $(x,y)=(1,0)$ entonces $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"Así, si su estrategia gana para las tres posibilidades, entonces\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1),$ and for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto implica que la estrategia pierde en el caso final $(x,y) = (1,1),$ donde ganar requiere que\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Por lo tanto, no puede existir una estrategia determinista que gane siempre.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Por otro lado, es fácil encontrar estrategias deterministas que ganen en tres de los cuatro casos, como $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"De esto concluimos que la probabilidad máxima de que Alice y Bob ganen usando una estrategia determinista es $3/4.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "Estrategias probabilistas {#probabilistic-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"Como acabamos de concluir, Alice y Bob no pueden hacer mejor que ganar el juego CHSH el 75% de las veces usando una estrategia determinista.\n"
"¿Pero qué pasa con una estrategia probabilista?\n"
"¿Podría ayudar a Alice y Bob usar aleatoriedad — incluyendo la posibilidad de *aleatoriedad compartida*, donde sus elecciones aleatorias están correlacionadas?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like (as was mentioned in the [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) lesson) probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Resulta que las estrategias probabilistas no ayudan en absoluto a aumentar la probabilidad de que Alice y Bob ganen.\n"
"Esto se debe a que toda estrategia probabilista puede verse alternativamente como una selección aleatoria de una estrategia determinista, igual que (como se menciónó en la lección de [Sistemas individuales](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction)) las operaciones probabilistas pueden verse como selecciones aleatorias de operaciones deterministas.\n"
"El promedio nunca es mayor que el máximo, por lo que se sigue que las estrategias probabilistas no ofrecen ninguna ventaja en términos de su probabilidad global de victoria.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do "
"using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Así, ganar con probabilidad $3/4$ es lo mejor que Alice y Bob pueden hacer "
"usando cualquier estrategia clásica, ya sea determinista o probabilista.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "Estrategia para el juego CHSH {#chsh-game-strategy}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"Una pregunta natural en este punto es si Alice y Bob pueden hacerlo mejor usando una estrategia *cuántica*.\n"
"En particular, si comparten un estado cuántico entrelazado como sugiere la siguiente figura, que podrían haber preparado antes de jugar el juego, ¿pueden aumentar su probabilidad de victoria?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game-entanglement.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Juego no local con entrelazamiento](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game-entanglement.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"La respuesta es sí, y ese es el punto principal del ejemplo y la razón por la que es tan interesante.\n"
"Así que veamos exactamente cómo Alice y Bob pueden hacerlo mejor en este juego usando entrelazamiento.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "Vectores y matrices necesarios {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lo primero que debemos hacer es definir un vector de estado de qubit $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ para cada número real\n"
"$\\theta$ (que pensaremos como un ángulo medido en radianes) de la siguiente forma.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "Aquí hay algunos ejemplos simples:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr ""
"También tenemos los siguientes ejemplos, que aparecen en el análisis de más "
"adelante:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two "
"of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Al observar la forma general, vemos que el producto interno entre dos "
"cualesquiera de estos vectores tiene esta fórmula:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"En detalle, como las entradas de estos vectores son solo números reales, no hay conjugados complejos de los cuales preocuparse:\n"
"el producto interno es el producto de los cosenos más el producto de los senos.\n"
"Usar una de las *fórmulas de adición de ángulos* de trigonometría conduce a la simplificación anterior.\n"
"Esta fórmula revela la interpretación geométrica del producto interno entre vectores unitarios reales como el coseno del ángulo entre ellos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these "
"vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar "
"expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr ""
"Si calculamos el producto interno del *producto tensorial* de dos "
"cualesquiera de estos vectores con el estado $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$, "
"obtenemos una expresión similar, excepto que tiene un $\\sqrt{2}$ en el "
"denominador:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but"
" for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nuestro interés en este producto interno en particular quedará claro en "
"breve, pero por ahora simplemente lo observamos como una fórmula.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, definamos una matriz unitaria $U_{\\theta}$ para cada ángulo"
" $\\theta$ de la siguiente manera.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Intuitivamente, esta matriz transforma $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ en $\\vert 0\\rangle$ y $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ en $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Para verificar que es una matriz unitaria, una observación clave es que los vectores $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ y $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ son ortogonales para todo ángulo $\\theta$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "Así, encontramos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "También podemos escribir esta matriz explícitamente como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Este es un ejemplo de una *matriz de rotación*, y específicamente rota vectores bidimensionales con entradas de números reales en un ángulo de $-\\theta$ alrededor del origen.\n"
"Si seguimos una convención estándar para nombrar y parametrizar rotaciones de diversas formas, tenemos\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ donde\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "Descripción de la estrategia {#strategy-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "Ahora podemos describir la estrategia cuántica.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a "
"qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the two "
"qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ "
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Configuración:** Alice y Bob comienzan el juego compartiendo un e-bit: "
"Alice tiene un qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob tiene un qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ y "
"juntos los dos qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ están en el estado "
"$\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Acciones de Alice:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question $x=0,$ she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si Alice recibe la pregunta $x=0,$ aplica $U_{0}$ a su qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question  $x=1,$ she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit"
" $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si Alice recibe la pregunta $x=1,$ aplica $U_{\\pi/4}$ a su qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  La operación que Alice realiza sobre $\\mathsf{A}$ puede describirse alternativamente así:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Alice applies this operation, she measures $\\mathsf{A}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets her answer $a$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Después de aplicar esta operación, Alice mide $\\mathsf{A}$ con una "
"medición en la base estándar y establece su respuesta $a$ como el resultado "
"de la medición.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Bob's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Acciones de Bob:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=0,$ he applies $U_{\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si Bob recibe la pregunta $y=0,$ aplica $U_{\\pi/8}$ a su qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=1,$ he applies $U_{-\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si Bob recibe la pregunta $y=1,$ aplica $U_{-\\pi/8}$ a su qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Like we did for Alice, we can express Bob's operation on $\\mathsf{B}$ like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Al igual que hicimos con Alice, podemos expresar la operación de Bob sobre $\\mathsf{B}$ así:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Bob applies this operation, he measures $\\mathsf{B}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets his answer $b$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Después de aplicar esta operación, Bob mide $\\mathsf{B}$ con una medición"
" en la base estándar y establece su respuesta $b$ como el resultado de la "
"medición.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes this strategy:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí hay un diagrama de circuito cuántico que describe esta estrategia:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/CHSH.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuito del juego CHSH](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/CHSH.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram we see two ordinary controlled gates, one for $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{\\pi/4}$ on the bottom.\n"
"We also have two gates that look like controlled gates, one for $U_{\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{0}$ on the bottom, except that the circle representing the control is not filled in.\n"
"This denotes a different type of controlled gate where the gate is performed if the control is set to $0$ (rather than $1$ like an ordinary controlled gate).\n"
"So, effectively, Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his qubit if $y=0$ and $U_{-\\pi/8}$ if $y=1;$\n"
"and Alice performs $U_0$ on her qubit if $x=0$ and $U_{\\pi/4}$ if $x=1,$ which is consistent with the description of the protocol in words above.\n"
msgstr ""
"En este diagrama vemos dos compuertas controladas ordinarias, una para $U_{-\\pi/8}$ en la parte superior y otra para $U_{\\pi/4}$ en la parte inferior.\n"
"También tenemos dos compuertas que parecen compuertas controladas, una para $U_{\\pi/8}$ arriba y otra para $U_{0}$ abajo, excepto que el círculo que representa el control no está relleno.\n"
"Esto denota un tipo diferente de compuerta controlada donde la compuerta se ejecuta si el control está en $0$ (en lugar de $1$ como en una compuerta controlada ordinaria).\n"
"Entonces, efectivamente, Bob aplica $U_{\\pi/8}$ a su qubit si $y=0$ y $U_{-\\pi/8}$ si $y=1;$\n"
"y Alice aplica $U_0$ a su qubit si $x=0$ y $U_{\\pi/4}$ si $x=1,$ lo cual es consistente con la descripción del protocolo en palabras anterior.\n"

